  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Tete landsbygdsel</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tete rural electrification - Construction and supervision</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Att m&#xf6;ta efterfr&#xe5;gan p&#xe5; elektricitet f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja den ekonomiska    och sociala utvecklingen i Mo&#xe7;ambique.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support economic and social development of Mozambique through      meeting the demand for electricity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tete Rural Electrification Project Agreement is under the overall agreement of Sofala Manica Tete (A2300075_51140042&#xa0;El: Sofala, Manica, Tete) that on 1 April 2004 and ended 30 June 2016. The total amount of the contribution is MSEK 46. Noting that the first payment was only in 2012. The overall agreement consisted&#xa0;of three separate&#xa0;contributions namely; Sofala Manica Tete Rural Electrification, Chibabava Buzi Rural Electrification and Tete Expansion. The purpose of this contribution is to electrify Tete specifically but the results are difficult to separate&#xa0;from the other two contributions as projects&apos; activities, financial account and reporting are intertwined.&#xa0;
Tete city was undergoing rapid expansion as a result of several mining developments. The demand for power, to establish new expansions areas are increasing as well as to support new infrastructure developments to cater for present and future expansion.The network needs to be reinforced in the following areas around Tete City; Josina Machel, Filipe Samuel Magaia, Mateus Sansao Mutemba, Francisco Manhanga and Samora Machel.
Based on the assumed needs of power in Tete City and the limitation of funds, the priority was to construct new main distribution lines and upgrade distribution transformers to at least overcome the actual demand of power in the above mentioned prioritized areas. The total construction scope of work of this part under the Sofala Manica Tete Project concerning Tete City consisted of:
&#x2022; Construction of 800m of 66/33kV double circuit Over Head Transmission Line (OHTL)&#x2022; Construction of 19 km of Mid Voltage (MV) Over Head Line (OHL) 33kV.&#x2022; Installation of 1x160kVA, 11x250kVA, 11x315kVA, 3 x 500kVA distribution transformers, (KVA= KiloVoltAmpere)&#x2022; Construction of 50 km of L V OHL 0,4 kV network, (KV=KiloVolt)&#x2022; Connection of 2200 new consumers.
The project objectives were achieved to the extent that of existing distribution network in medium voltage and low voltage was expanded within Tete City and surrounding rural areas, hence to provide quality and more reliable and trustworthy&#xa0;electrical power supply to both existing and new consumers.</narrative>
  </description>
